<title>FINLAND: FINNISH 2010 BOND YIELDS 6.59 PCT AT AUCTION.</title>
<headline>FINNISH 2010 BOND YIELDS 6.59 PCT AT AUCTION.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following issue of the</p>
<p>S1/95 bond was announced by the State Treasury Office:</p>
<p> ISSUER:				 Republic of Finland</p>
<p> MATURITY:			     15-10-2010</p>
<p> COUPON:				 8.25 PCT</p>
<p> AUCTION YIELD:			6.59 PCT</p>
<p> PRICE:				  114.35</p>
<p> AUCTION AMOUNT			FIM 102 MLN</p>
<p> BID AMOUNT:			   FIM 244 MLN</p>
<p> PAYMENT FREQUENCY:		  YEARLY  NOTES:</p>
<p>After this auction, the outstanding amount is 3,765 million</p>
<p>markka.</p>
<p>The previous auction of the bond raised 60 million markka</p>
<p>at a price of 113.40 and a yield of 6.70 percent.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-6805 0240, news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
